Here is how you can create a string parameter with a default value in Go:

```go
func greet(name string) {
    if name == "" {
        name = "Guest"
    }
    fmt.Println("Hello, " + name)
}
```

Alternatively, you can use a pointer to a string to distinguish between an empty string and a nil value, allowing the caller to explicitly pass an empty string if desired:

```go
func greet(name *string) {
    if name == nil {
        name = new(string)
        *name = "Guest"
    }
    fmt.Println("Hello, " + *name)
}
```

Or, using a struct with a default value (common in configuration):

```go
type Config struct {
    Name string
}

func NewConfig() Config {
    return Config{Name: "DefaultName"}
}
```

